WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:02.540
This is the Strategya Catalog.

2
00:00:02.540 --> 00:00:03.750
Here's how to read it,

3
00:00:03.750 --> 00:00:05.240
card by card.

4
00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:07.710
Strategies come in three tiers,

5
00:00:07.710 --> 00:00:09.780
entry, intermediate, and expert.

6
00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:12.070
Each tier includes the ones below it,

7
00:00:12.070 --> 00:00:13.760
so expert has everything.

8
00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:16.900
Every card opens with today's position.

9
00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:19.890
Here, Bitcoin is 100% in cash.

10
00:00:19.890 --> 00:00:22.140
A card can also be long or short,

11
00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:23.600
like this one.

12
00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:26.410
Long plus short strategies are in early access.

13
00:00:26.410 --> 00:00:28.790
Their results are still preliminary.

14
00:00:28.790 --> 00:00:31.640
Below the position, whether it changed today

15
00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:34.230
and the last change with its date.

16
00:00:34.230 --> 00:00:36.280
Here, from Bitcoin to cash,

17
00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:38.080
13 days ago.

18
00:00:38.080 --> 00:00:39.340
Then, the last trade,

19
00:00:39.340 --> 00:00:41.480
its result, how long it lasted,

20
00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:43.560
and the price it closed at.

21
00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:47.140
On rotation strategies, which move between several assets,

22
00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:48.880
you will see cash to cash,

23
00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:51.160
the result of the whole stay in the market,

24
00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:53.290
across every asset it held.

25
00:00:53.290 --> 00:00:55.770
On the right, the live price.

26
00:00:55.770 --> 00:00:57.050
Tap price chart.

27
00:00:57.050 --> 00:00:59.560
The chart shows the daily closes of the asset,

28
00:00:59.560 --> 00:01:01.680
orange while the strategy held it,

29
00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:03.900
green while it sat in cash.

30
00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:05.550
You can choose the window,

31
00:01:05.550 --> 00:01:07.040
six months, one year,

32
00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:09.600
two years, or since 2023.

33
00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:11.490
The line at the bottom tells you how the

34
00:01:11.490 --> 00:01:13.730
asset did over that window and how much of

35
00:01:13.730 --> 00:01:16.140
the time the strategy was in position.

36
00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:18.620
Now tap plus to open the full card.

37
00:01:18.620 --> 00:01:22.360
First, the strategy against simply holding the asset.

38
00:01:22.360 --> 00:01:24.860
Same $1,000, same start date.

39
00:01:24.860 --> 00:01:28.400
The strategy turned it into $6,768,

40
00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:33.180
holding Bitcoin into $4,852.

41
00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:36.150
The multiplier says the same thing in one number,

42
00:01:36.150 --> 00:01:38.790
6.8 times against 4.9.

43
00:01:38.790 --> 00:01:42.580
Max drawdown is the worst drop along the way.

44
00:01:42.580 --> 00:01:44.750
13% for the strategy,

45
00:01:44.750 --> 00:01:46.640
49% for holding.

46
00:01:46.640 --> 00:01:49.480
CAGR is the average yearly growth,

47
00:01:49.480 --> 00:01:53.110
and MAR divides that growth by the drawdown.

48
00:01:53.110 --> 00:01:54.800
Return per unit of pain.

49
00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:56.150
Higher is better.

50
00:01:56.150 --> 00:01:57.480
You can switch the window up

51
00:01:57.480 --> 00:01:58.880
here and read the longer,

52
00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:01.900
harder stretch since 2018 just below.

53
00:02:01.900 --> 00:02:04.870
Tap any info icon for a plain English definition.

54
00:02:04.870 --> 00:02:07.360
Next, the position history,

55
00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:08.780
a ribbon of every day.

56
00:02:08.780 --> 00:02:10.570
Orange when it held Bitcoin,

57
00:02:10.570 --> 00:02:12.070
green when it was in cash.

58
00:02:12.070 --> 00:02:14.540
Tap a band to read that trade.

59
00:02:14.540 --> 00:02:16.200
Open the replay to watch

60
00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:18.270
the backtest bar by bar.

61
00:02:18.270 --> 00:02:19.900
Green is the strategy,

62
00:02:19.900 --> 00:02:23.270
orange is holding, both from $1,000.

63
00:02:23.270 --> 00:02:25.690
Press play or step through at one,

64
00:02:25.690 --> 00:02:27.570
five, or 20 times speed.

65
00:02:27.570 --> 00:02:29.270
The line above tells you what

66
00:02:29.270 --> 00:02:30.900
the card said on that day.

67
00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:32.760
Open the trade history,

68
00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:34.480
every trade on one line.

69
00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:36.560
When it bought, when it sold,

70
00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:39.270
at what prices, and what it returned.

71
00:02:39.270 --> 00:02:41.110
The cash stretches are listed too,

72
00:02:41.110 --> 00:02:43.400
so you can see how long the rule waited.

73
00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:46.390
Then the statistics, like a strategy tester.

74
00:02:46.390 --> 00:02:50.460
Total P&L, everything the strategy made over the window.

75
00:02:50.460 --> 00:02:51.480
Year to date.

76
00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:52.480
Win rate.

77
00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:55.960
How many trades closed with a gain? Profit factor.

78
00:02:55.960 --> 00:02:58.460
Dollars won for every dollar lost.

79
00:02:58.460 --> 00:03:01.220
Average monthly return, average holding time,

80
00:03:01.220 --> 00:03:03.980
and the typical winner against the typical loser.

81
00:03:03.980 --> 00:03:06.220
Each number has its own window selector,

82
00:03:06.220 --> 00:03:07.610
and its own info icon.

83
00:03:07.610 --> 00:03:08.800
And at the bottom,

84
00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:10.630
every month and every year.

85
00:03:10.630 --> 00:03:11.980
Green for a gain,

86
00:03:11.980 --> 00:03:12.840
red for a loss,

87
00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:15.040
and the year's total on the right.

88
00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:17.550
Cards update every day after the close.

89
00:03:17.550 --> 00:03:19.450
Midnight UTC for crypto,

90
00:03:19.450 --> 00:03:22.110
after the NYSE close for stocks.

91
00:03:22.110 --> 00:03:24.620
Everything here is a simulated backtest.

92
00:03:24.620 --> 00:03:27.880
Not real performance, and not investment advice.

